## 4 STATUTORY AND REGULATORY REQUIREMENTS

The top management shall ensure compliance to all applicable statutory and regulatory requirements.

## 5 GENERAL REQUIREMENTS

The top management shall:

- a) adopt sustainable practices at the campus and accommodation facilities, wherever applicable;
- b) ensure availability of resources to facilitate teaching and scientific research work;
- c) maintain optimal temperature and humidity level for comfort of users;
- d) promote innovation and incubation activities such as maker space or tinkering lab for members;
- e) establish and implement guidelines/SOPs for clean classrooms, laboratories, libraries, corridors, dining areas, water tanks, toilets, trash yards and all other parts of campus;




- f) establish building maintenance plan and its implementation to ensure safety and functionality of premises;
- g) establish and implement protocols for responding to emergencies including natural and manmade disasters;
- h) ensure availability of multi-purpose spaces/facilities for extracurricular activities, student clubs or societies, personal development, technical or cultural events and social engagements;
- j) provide adequate infrastructure for academic counselling and psychological counselling;
- k) promote accessibility and inclusivity for all members including elderly and especially abled members; and
- m) display adequate signages at prominent and strategic locations within the campus to ensure easy navigation for members, enhanced accessibility and safety and compliance with statutory and safety regulations.

