- d) ensure availability of contact numbers of nodal officer appointed by educational organization in case of health emergency.

### 6.7  Classroom and Laboratory

The organization in its classrooms and laboratories shall:

a) provide classrooms having space of at least 1.1 m2 for each learner;


- b) provide labs and testing facility as per the course curriculum;
- c) ensure accessibility to specially abled learner and members such as adjustable workstations and tactile markers;
- d) establish and implement safety protocols and guidelines for handling hazardous materials and conducting experiments safely in labs;
- e) establish a maintenance plan and implement it for lab equipment to ensure equipment functionality and safety compliance; and
- f) segregate and dispose of classroom and laboratory waste safely and scientifically.
NOTE — Refer Annex B for guidelines on advanced infrastructure in classrooms and laboratory.


### 6.8  Communication

The educational organization shall:

- a) install communication facilities such as telephone lines for internal and external communication at appropriate locations;
- b) install CCTV at the entrance gate(s), administrative blocks and other prominent locations, where appropriate;
- c) determine and make available other communication infrastructure such as computers, internet, teleconferencing, walkie-talkie sets;
- d) make available mobile phones with key persons especially officials responsible to maintain security in the premises; and
- e) display phone numbers of key persons and facilities at prominent locations such as entrance gates, all administrative/ accommodation buildings, health clinics, infirmaries.

### 6.9  Maintenance and Complaint Handling

The educational organization shall:

- a) establish a maintenance department for redressal of complaints including repair and replacement of installed appliances and associated accessories within organization;
- b) establish a mechanism for receipt of complaints;
- c) constitute a maintenance team for daily complaints;
- d) maintain records of complaint received and action taken;
- e) ensure competence of maintenance staff;
- f) keep inventory of components needed frequently for repair;
- g) keep record of consumables;
- h) prepare a preventive maintenance plan for the facilities in the campus including equipment, appliances, furniture, building; and
- j) plan for painting/whitewashing including minor repairs of buildings in the premises.

### 6.10  Hygiene

The educational organization shall:

- a) make available trained manpower for housekeeping;
- b) plan for periodic cleaning and dusting;
- c) provide dustbins (separate for dry and wet waste) at appropriate locations;
- d) provide for collection and management of solid waste; and
- e) provide for management and safe disposal of hazardous waste.

