### 7.3  Dining Services

The RGC shall establish a dining services management committee (DSMC) consisting of at least one warden and one enrolled elected member from the respective residential blocks for the effective implementation of dining services.

The DSMC shall:

- a) ensure in-dining facility offers healthy and flexible meal plan;
- b) establish and implement policy on in- dining services;
- c) ensure availability of adequate spaces and seating arrangement for dining facility for members and visitors;
- d) ensure availability of well-equipped kitchen, storage areas, washing area for utensils, hand-wash area, toilets for
members and kitchen staff and similar functional areas;

- e) conduct regular briefing and periodic training sessions to educate kitchen staff on proper cleaning techniques, personal hygiene and food safety protocols;
- f) establish and implement food safety protocols and conduct regular inspections to maintain food quality and hygiene in kitchen and dining area;
- g) take regular feedback from members in structured format and take action, where required, to ensure hygiene and quality of food; and
- h) ensure safe segregation, handling and disposal of kitchen waste.
NOTE — The educational organization should encourage the use of local and organic ingredients for food preparation.


## 8 LIBRARY SERVICES

The educational organisation shall:

- a) appoint competent person as library in- charge;
- b) maintain sufficient and competent staff to provide basic library services;
- c) provide adequate space and comfortable seating facilities;
- d) designate spaces for different literary resources such as books, new arrivals, journals and study areas;
- e) provide appropriate area(s) dedicated as silent zones for reading;
- f) establish mechanisms for delivery and return of books, publications, catalogues, etc;
- g) use ICT tool to facilitate online database and digital resources;
- h) ensure regular surveillance and security measures to protect library resources and maintain a disciplined learning environment; and
- j) take regular feedback and complaint handling system specific to library services.

