## 9 SERVICES FOR MEMBERS WITH SPECIAL NEEDS

The educational organizations shall ensure:

- a) availability of accessible facilities such as ramps, elevators/lifts;




- b) that restrooms are equipped with grab bars, lowered sinks and accessible stalls to accommodate members with mobility challenges;
- c) availability of designated parking spaces with appropriate signage and pathways;
- d) training of faculty and staff on disability awareness and inclusive teaching practices; and
- e) the conduct of adequate awareness programs and workshops to educate students about disability rights, inclusion and ways to support their peers with disabilities.
NOTE —  Refer to IS 4963 for guidance on accessibility in buildings.


## 10 SUSTAINABILITY APPROACH

The educational organization shall establish a campus specific environmental policy to sensitize the issue of sustainability. The policy shall:

- a) design and develop adequate landscape areas to promote greenery with native biodiversity and outdoor learning opportunities;
- b) encourage energy-efficient technologies integrating renewable energy techniques in campus;
- c) encourage implementation of waste segregation systems, use of recycle bins throughout the campus; and
- d) promote educational initiatives such as environmental sensitization programs to foster a culture of environmental responsibility among members.
NOTE — Refer IS/ISO 14001 and IS/ISO 50001 for guidance on environmental and energy management respectively.


## 11 SAFETY AND SECURITY

The educational organisation shall constitute a committee to establish guidelines for safety and security of campus and accommodation facilities. The guidelines shall, but not limited to, address the following:

- a) compliance with norms laid by national and regional regulatory bodies (such as building bylaws, anti-ragging, POSH, POCSO and other relevant regulation) for safety and security on the campus;
- b) compliance of regulations like cyber security, anti-bullying, anti-racism;
- c) establish surveillance monitoring and its implementation on the campus;
- d) select locations to station the security personnel;
- e) prohibit the consumption, possession, distribution, sale or exchange of banned substances;
- f) establish and implement plans to conduct safety inspections and risk assessments to identify and   mitigate potential hazards; and
- g) compliance with fire safety norms as prescribed by appropriate authority.
