## ANNEX C

(Clause 11)

SAFETY AND SECURITY GUIDELINES

C-1 ENTRY AND EXIT

The educational organization shall record and maintain entry and exit timing of the members, residents and visitors. The following should be considered to maintain the safety and security at the entry and exit of the campus:

- a) The perimeter of the campus should be secured to control access to the premises;
- b) A record of all staff reporting for duty must be maintained;
- c) A visitor pass is to be given, and signed by
the person who has been met;

- d) Every person on the premises should have a valid identity card or a visitor pass; and
- e) If a side gate exists, it shall be manned by a security guard who shall record all entries and exits in a register.
C-2 FIRE READINESS

The educational organization shall ensure:

- a) installation of fire alarm system on the campus;




- b) functionality of fire extinguishers and availability of trained staff to operate them;
- c) safety of the electrical appliances;
- d) provide clear access to the fire exit (door);
- e) fire drills are conducted once a quarter;
- f) display fire exit plan is at prominent locations and conduct mock drills at regular intervals;
- g) evacuation plan is clearly visible and accurate; and
- h) availability of designated safety office.

## ANNEX D

(Clause 7.2)

ADDITIONAL SERVICE REQUIREMENTS SPECIFIC TO ACCOMMODATION

D-1 LIST OF PROHIBITED ACTIVITIES IN ACCOMMODATION OF CAMPUS PREMISES

In the hostel premises, the following activities shall be strictly prohibited:

- a) Smoking;
- b) Consumption of alcoholic drinks;
- c) Gambling;
- d) Intimidation or violence;
- e) Entering the hostel premises in an intoxicated state;
- f) Using abusive languages;
- g) Cooking inside the room;
- h) Disruption of property;
- j) Any act that prevents, disrupts, or disturbs regular academic activity;
- k) Unlawful assembly and rioting;
- m) Public nuisance;
- n) Violation of moral code of conduct;
- p) Extortion;
- q) Trespassing;
- r) Any act of abuse both physical or/and mental;
- s) Attempts to commit any or all the above- mentioned offenses; and
- t) Threat to commit any or all the above- mentioned offenses.

